let __v_189 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"flat white\",\"flat whites\"]},\"A flat white is a double shot of espresso under a thin layer of steamed milk, about 160ml in the cup.\",\"Strong and milky at once: the coffee is at the front and the milk softens it without hiding it, and the foam is a thin glossy layer rather than a cap you eat with a spoon.\",\"It is a morning coffee on its own. With food, a plain croissant or a slice of toast beats anything sweet, because the milk and the sugar fight.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"latte\",\"lattes\",\"caffe latte\"]},\"A latte is one or two shots of espresso topped up with a lot of steamed milk, in a tall glass or a big cup.\",\"Milky and mild: the milk is most of the drink and the coffee is a soft bitterness behind it, with a thin foam on top. Ask for it with an extra shot if you want to taste the coffee.\",\"It is milky enough to drink with breakfast or a sweet thing, and it goes flat with a sharp lemon cake or anything acidic.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cappuccino\",\"cappuccinos\",\"capuccino\"]},\"A cappuccino is an espresso with equal parts steamed milk and thick foam, usually in a smaller cup than a latte.\",\"It is a third coffee, a third milk and a third foam, so the first sip is dry foam and the coffee is stronger and shorter than in a latte. In Italy it is a morning drink, not one for after a meal.\",\"Best with something plain at breakfast - a pastry or a biscuit - and it is the wrong coffee to sit beside a meal.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"americano\",\"americanos\",\"caffe americano\",\"long black\"]},\"An americano is one or two shots of espresso with hot water added, so it is black coffee made in a cup.\",\"Black and clean, with the coffee's bitterness and no milk to soften it: longer and less intense than an espresso, because the water thins it. A long black is the same thing with the water in the cup first, which keeps more of the crema.\",\"It is the coffee for a meal or for a long sit, and the one to order if milk upsets you.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"espresso\",\"espressos\",\"expresso\",\"double espresso\",\"short black\"]},\"An espresso is a small, strong shot of coffee forced through finely ground beans by a machine, about 25 to 30ml.\",\"Concentrated and bittersweet with a thick crema on top: coffee, caramel and a dry finish, drunk in two or three sips. It has less caffeine than a mug of filter coffee, not more.\",\"It is the finish to a meal rather than a drink with one, and a small sweet thing beside it is the Italian way.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"macchiato\",\"macchiatos\",\"latte macchiato\"]},\"A macchiato is an espresso with a spoonful of milk foam on top. A latte macchiato is the other way round: a glass of hot milk with a shot poured into it.\",\"An espresso macchiato tastes of the coffee with a soft, slightly sweet top; a latte macchiato is milky with a coffee layer sitting above it, so the first sip is coffee and the rest is warm milk.\",\"A macchiato is a two-minute coffee on its own; the latte macchiato is a breakfast drink.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mocha\",\"mochas\",\"caffe mocha\",\"mocha latte\"]},\"A mocha is a latte with chocolate syrup or powder stirred into the espresso before the milk goes in.\",\"Sweet and chocolatey, coffee second: it is closer to a hot chocolate with a kick than to a coffee, and the chocolate hides a weak shot. Ask for half the syrup if you want to taste the coffee at all.\",\"It is a pudding as much as a drink, so it wants no cake beside it.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"filter coffee\",\"filter\",\"cafetiere\",\"french press\",\"drip coffee\",\"black coffee\"]},\"Filter coffee is ground coffee steeped in hot water and then filtered out, through paper in a dripper or a metal mesh in a cafetiere.\",\"Cleaner and lighter than an espresso, with the fruit and the acidity of the bean still in it: it tastes of tea and fruit as much as of coffee, and it goes bitter if it is left to stew on a hot plate.\",\"It is the drink for a second cup, and it takes milk and food better than an espresso does.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cold brew\",\"cold brew coffee\"]},\"Cold brew is ground coffee steeped in cold water for 12 to 18 hours and then strained, and served over ice.\",\"Round and low in acid, sweeter than hot-brewed coffee with almost none of the sharpness, and it is stronger in caffeine than the same volume of filter coffee because the ratio is concentrated.\",\"It is a summer drink: neat over ice, or cut with milk like a latte.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"green tea\"]},\"Green tea is unfermented tea leaf, brewed at about 80C rather than boiling.\",\"Grassy and light, with a sweetness at the back and a slight bitterness or astringency if it is left to steep - the leaves keep giving, so a second brew is softer than the first.\",\"It goes with rice, fish and anything light, and it is the drink to have with sushi.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"earl grey\",\"earl gray\",\"earl grey tea\"]},\"Earl grey is black tea scented with bergamot, the citrus oil from a bitter orange.\",\"Black tea first, then the bergamot on top: floral and perfumed, and it turns soapy if the milk is heavy or the bag is left in too long.\",\"It wants a slice of lemon rather than milk, and a plain biscuit or a scone.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"matcha\",\"matcha tea\",\"matcha latte\"]},\"Matcha is green tea leaf ground to a powder and whisked into hot water, so the whole leaf is drunk rather than steeped and thrown away.\",\"Vegetal and savoury, like spinach and fresh grass, with a bitterness that stays in the mouth. In a latte the milk turns it sweet and soft, and the colour is the point as much as the taste.\",\"It is good with anything sweet and milky, and it fights with citrus.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"chai\",\"chai tea\",\"chai latte\",\"masala chai\"]},\"Chai is black tea boiled with milk, sugar and whole spices - cardamom, ginger, cinnamon, cloves - so it is a spiced milky tea rather than tea with a flavour.\",\"Warm and sweet, with the spices arriving after the tea: ginger heat, cardamom and clove behind the milk. A chai latte in a coffee shop is the same idea with more sugar and foam.\",\"It is a winter drink and it takes a biscuit or something fried and savoury.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"prosecco\"]},\"Prosecco is a sparkling white wine from northern Italy, made in a tank rather than in the bottle, which keeps it cheap and fruity.\",\"Light and fizzy with green apple, pear and a little white flower: it is off-dry rather than sweet, and the bubbles make it feel fresher and less alcoholic than it is. Drink it young - it does not improve in the bottle.\",\"It goes with salty and fried things - crisps, olives, fried fish - and with fruit desserts; it is the wrong glass for a steak.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"champagne\",\"sparkling wine\",\"cava\",\"cremant\",\"cremant de loire\"]},\"Champagne is sparkling wine from the Champagne region of France, fermented a second time in the bottle, which is what the price pays for. Cava and cremant are made the same way elsewhere.\",\"Tighter and more yeasty than prosecco: brioche and toast from the time on the lees, with a sharper acidity and a finer bubble, and the best of it is dry rather than sweet.\",\"It goes with oysters, fried food and salty nuts, and with a roast chicken as well as with a celebration.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"red wine\"]},\"Red wine is wine fermented with the skins of the grapes, which is where the colour and the tannin come from.\",\"From light and juicy to heavy and drying depending on the grape: the tannin is the grip that dries your mouth, and it is what makes a young red taste harsh with nothing to eat.\",\"It goes with red meat, stews and hard cheese, and badly with anything vinegary or very spicy.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"white wine\"]},\"White wine is wine fermented without the skins, so it is pale and lower in tannin.\",\"From bone dry and citrusy to sweet and honeyed: the cool-climate ones taste of lemon and green apple and the warm ones of peach and melon, and oak adds vanilla and butter.\",\"It goes with fish, chicken, salads and soft cheese, and a dry one is the safer glass with food than a red.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rose\",\"rosé\",\"rose wine\",\"pink wine\"]},\"Rosé is wine that spent a few hours with the red grape skins, enough for the colour and not for the tannin.\",\"Fresh and dry, usually with strawberry, watermelon and a little citrus, and served cold. The pale Provencal kind is the driest; the darker, sweeter ones are a different drink.\",\"It goes with salads, grilled vegetables, chicken and anything you would eat outdoors.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"lager\",\"lagers\"]},\"Lager is beer brewed with a bottom-fermenting yeast at a cold temperature and then stored, which is where the clean taste comes from.\",\"Crisp and cold, lightly bitter and dry at the end, with very little fruit: the point is how clean it is, which is why it goes with almost everything.\",\"It goes with a curry, fish and chips, pizza and a hot day. The colder it is the less you taste it, so a good one is served cool rather than iced.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ipa\",\"ipas\",\"india pale ale\",\"pale ale\"]},\"An IPA is a heavily hopped pale ale; the hops were originally there to keep the beer on the voyage to India.\",\"Bitter and citrusy or piney, with the hop flavour at the front and a long bitter finish. A hazy New England IPA is softer and fruitier, and a pale ale is the same idea turned down.\",\"It goes with a burger, fried chicken or a strong cheese, and it flattens a delicate fish.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stout\",\"stouts\",\"guinness\",\"porter\"]},\"Stout is a dark beer brewed with roasted barley, which is where the coffee and chocolate come from.\",\"Roasted and smooth: coffee, dark chocolate and a dry, bitter finish, and the creamy sort is served on nitrogen so the head is thick and the bubbles are tiny.\",\"It goes with oysters, stews and chocolate, and it is a meal in itself compared with a lager.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cider\",\"ciders\"]},\"Cider is fermented apple juice. In the UK it is alcoholic and still or sparkling; in the US the word usually means the cloudy juice.\",\"From bone dry and tannic to sweet and appley: the dry ones taste of the fruit and the skin and the sweet ones of juice, and the strength varies more than with beer.\",\"It goes with pork, cheese and anything with apple in it, and it is the drink for a pub garden.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gin\",\"gin and tonic\"]},\"Gin is a clear spirit distilled with juniper and then other botanicals, and a gin and tonic is that with tonic water and ice.\",\"Juniper first, then whatever the maker put in - citrus peel, coriander, angelica, sometimes cucumber or violet. The tonic adds bitterness and sugar, so a G&T tastes of the tonic as much as the gin.\",\"It goes with olives, salted nuts and fried fish; it is a before-dinner drink.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"whisky\",\"whiskey\",\"scotch\",\"bourbon\",\"single malt\"]},\"Whisky is a spirit distilled from grain and aged in wood, which is where the colour and most of the flavour come from. Scotch and bourbon are the two most people meet.\",\"From light and honeyed to smoky and medicinal: bourbon is sweeter and tastes of vanilla and caramel from the new oak, and a peated Scotch of smoke and tar. A drop of water opens it up rather than diluting it.\",\"It goes with dark chocolate, blue cheese and a fire, and it is not a drink to have with a meal.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"vodka\"]},\"Vodka is a spirit distilled to as close to pure alcohol and water as the law allows, then cut to strength.\",\"Almost nothing, which is the point: clean and slightly sweet at the front and hot at the back, with the flavour coming from whatever it is mixed with. A cheap one tastes of the distillery and a good one of nothing.\",\"It goes with tonic, tomato juice or a martini glass, and with salty things.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rum\"]},\"Rum is distilled from sugar cane or its molasses. The clear kind is unaged; the dark kind is aged in wood.\",\"Sweet and round, with vanilla, caramel and sometimes a burnt sugar edge; a white rum is lighter and drier, and an aged one is closer to a whisky in weight.\",\"It goes with lime and ginger beer, and with anything you would put brown sugar on.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"beer\",\"beers\",\"a pint of beer\",\"real ale\"]},\"Beer is brewed from grain, usually barley, with hops for bitterness and yeast for the alcohol.\",\"From light and crisp to dark and roasted, depending on the malt: the hops give the bitterness and the fruit, the malt gives the sweetness and the colour. Most beer is between 4 and 5.5 per cent, and served colder than wine.\",\"It goes with fried food, pizza, curry and a hot afternoon, and a hoppy one with a burger.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coffee\",\"coffees\",\"a coffee\"]},\"Coffee is the roasted and ground seed of a fruit, brewed with hot water.\",\"Bitter and acidic at once, with the roast on top: darker roasts taste of chocolate and toast, lighter ones of fruit and citrus, and the bitterness is the part that survives milk and sugar.\",\"It goes with anything sweet in the morning and with nothing much after a meal, which is why a small espresso is the usual finish.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tea\",\"teas\",\"a cup of tea\",\"builder's tea\"]},\"Tea is the leaf of one plant, Camellia sinensis, brewed in hot water; how it is processed decides whether it is black, green or white.\",\"Tannin first: dry and slightly astringent, with the flavour of the leaf behind it, and it goes bitter if it is left in the water too long. Milk softens the tannin, which is why a strong tea takes milk and a delicate one does not.\",\"It goes with a biscuit, a slice of cake or a fried breakfast, and it is the drink for bad news.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"oat milk\",\"oat drink\",\"oatly\",\"oat milk latte\"]},\"Oat milk is oats soaked, blended and strained, with an enzyme step that turns some of the starch to sugar, which is why it is the plant milk that foams.\",\"Oaty and faintly sweet like the milk left at the bottom of a bowl of porridge, with a creaminess that comes from the oats rather than fat. In coffee the ordinary sort splits and tastes of cardboard; a barista version has oil added and holds.\",\"It goes with coffee, cereal and anything oaty or banana-flavoured, and it curdles in a strong acid the way no dairy milk does.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"baileys\",\"irish cream\",\"cream liqueur\"]},\"Irish cream is whiskey, cream and sugar, homogenised so the cream does not separate - Baileys is the one everybody means.\",\"Sweet and thick, of whiskey and cream with a chocolate edge: it is a pudding in a glass rather than a drink, and the alcohol is under the sugar.\",\"It goes over ice, in coffee and over vanilla ice cream. Do not put it in a citrus drink - the acid splits the cream - and keep the bottle in the fridge once it is open.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"negroni\",\"negronis\"]},\"A negroni is equal parts gin, Campari and sweet vermouth, stirred over ice and poured over a big cube with a strip of orange peel.\",\"Bitter first, then sweet and herby: the Campari is the grapefruit-and-rhubarb bitterness, the vermouth is the sweetness behind it, and the gin is the spine rather than the flavour.\",\"It is an aperitivo before dinner rather than a drink with food, and it is strong: about 24 per cent once mixed, so one is the usual.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"aperol spritz\",\"spritz\",\"spritzes\",\"aperol\"]},\"A spritz is three parts prosecco, two parts Aperol and a splash of soda, over ice in a wine glass with a slice of orange.\",\"Light, fizzy and bittersweet - orange and rhubarb from the Aperol, the wine behind it - and much weaker than it looks, because most of the glass is ice and prosecco.\",\"It is a drink for a hot afternoon or before dinner. It goes with salty things - olives, crisps, a bowl of nuts - and nothing sweet.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kombucha\"]},\"Kombucha is sweet tea fermented with a culture of yeast and bacteria, which turns the sugar into acid and a little alcohol.\",\"Sour and slightly fizzy, like a vinegar you can drink, with the fruit or herb it was brewed with on top: it is the sourness, not the sweetness, that most people notice first.\",\"It goes with sushi and anything rich, and it is a good stand-in for a beer at lunch.\"]}]}")?;
