let __v_305 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$dict\":[[{\"$tuple\":[\"cappuccino\",\"latte\"]},\"A latte is the milkier of the two: a lot of steamed milk with a thin foam on top, in a bigger cup. A cappuccino is a third coffee, a third milk and a third foam, in a smaller cup, so it is drier to drink and tastes more of the coffee.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"flat white\",\"latte\"]},\"A flat white is smaller and stronger: a double shot under a thin, glossy layer of milk. A latte is mostly milk. Order the flat white for the coffee and the latte for something mild and long.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"cappuccino\",\"flat white\"]},\"Both are small and strong. The flat white has thinner, glossier milk and no foam cap; the cappuccino is a third foam, so the first sip is dry and there is less milk under it.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"americano\",\"espresso\"]},\"An americano is an espresso with hot water added: the same coffee, a longer drink, and much less intense. An espresso is the 25 to 30ml shot on its own, with a thick crema.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"champagne\",\"prosecco\"]},\"Champagne is fermented a second time in the bottle, so it tastes of brioche and toast with a sharper acidity; prosecco is made in a tank, so it is fruitier, lighter and cheaper. Both are dry, and prosecco is the easier one to drink.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"ale\",\"lager\"]},\"Lager is fermented cold with a bottom yeast, so it is clean, crisp and lightly bitter. An ale is fermented warm, so it tastes fruitier and more bitter from the hops.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"ipa\",\"lager\"]},\"An IPA is far hoppier - bitter, citrusy or piney, with a long finish - and usually stronger. A lager is clean and light, and the point of it is that it tastes of very little.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"cider\",\"lager\"]},\"Cider is fermented apple juice, so it tastes of fruit and is often sweeter; beer is brewed from grain, so it tastes of hops and malt. Dry cider is the one closest to a lager in weight.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"red wine\",\"white wine\"]},\"Red is fermented with the grape skins, which gives it the colour and the tannin that dries your mouth; white has no skins, so it is lighter in body and tastes of citrus, apple and stone fruit. Reds suit red meat, whites suit fish and chicken.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"green tea\",\"black tea\",\"earl grey\"]},\"Green tea is unfermented leaf brewed at about 80C, so it is grassy and light. Black tea is fully oxidised and brewed boiling, so it is darker and maltier and takes milk; earl grey is black tea with bergamot oil on it.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"gin\",\"vodka\"]},\"Gin is vodka with juniper and other botanicals distilled in, so it tastes of something. Vodka is distilled to taste of almost nothing, which is why it is the one you mix.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"whisky\",\"vodka\"]},\"Whisky is grain spirit aged in wood, so it is coloured and tastes of vanilla, caramel or smoke; vodka is unaged and filtered to be neutral. Whisky is sipped and vodka is usually mixed.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"matcha\",\"green tea\"]},\"Matcha is green tea leaf ground to a powder and whisked into the water, so you drink the whole leaf: it is stronger, creamier and more bitter than green tea, which is the leaf steeped and taken out.\"],[{\"$tuple\":[\"cappuccino\",\"flat white\",\"mocha\"]},\"A mocha is a latte with chocolate in it: sweet, and coffee second. A flat white is the strongest of the milky coffees and a cappuccino is the foamiest.\"]]}")?;
